sequenceDiagram
%% Overheard - what happens when a user clicks "Collect feedback".
%% Exactly two model calls per run: one to plan, one to classify. Everything
%% between them is ordinary retrieval, deduplication and aggregation.
%%
%% Written for maximum renderer compatibility:
%%   - comments sit AFTER the diagram declaration, not before it
%%   - rect uses rgb(), since "transparent" needs a recent Mermaid
%%   - participant, not actor
%%   - plain hyphens, no em-dashes
    autonumber
    participant User
    participant UI as React Dashboard
    participant API as FastAPI
    participant SB as Supabase
    participant GPT as OpenAI gpt-5.6-sol
    participant SRC as Source Adapters
    participant ES as Elasticsearch

    User->>UI: Click "Collect feedback" (depth: standard)
    UI->>API: POST /products/:id/ingestions

    API->>SB: Validate JWT, load product under user token
    Note over SB: Row-level security enforces tenancy.<br/>Another org id returns 404.
    API->>SB: Insert ingestion_job (status: running)

    rect rgb(38, 38, 46)
    Note over API,GPT: Model call 1 of 2 - planning
    API->>GPT: Product name + source capabilities
    GPT-->>API: Chosen sources and queries per source
    Note over GPT: Steam for a game, not for headphones.<br/>Short keywords for Steam and HN,<br/>natural language for YouTube.
    end

    Note over API: If planning fails, a rule-based plan runs.<br/>The pipeline never depends on the model.

    par Collected in parallel
        API->>SRC: Hacker News - Algolia, 10 pages
    and
        API->>SRC: YouTube - verify title names product, then comments
    and
        API->>SRC: Steam - resolve app id, cursor-paginate reviews
    and
        API->>SRC: Browserbase - search, fetch, split into paragraphs
    and
        API->>SRC: Lemmy - 3 federated instances
    end
    SRC-->>API: SourceDocument list - one shape from every source

    Note over API: Clean: duplicate id, duplicate text hash,<br/>junk filter. Rejects kept with reasons.
    Note over API: Normalize: attach tenancy, hash the author.<br/>Usernames are never stored.

    rect rgb(38, 38, 46)
    Note over API,GPT: Model call 2 of 2 - classification
    API->>GPT: Batches of 10 comments, 12 in flight
    GPT-->>API: relevance, sentiment, intent, issues, summary
    Note over GPT: Rejects "first!! who else watching in 2026"<br/>as about the video, not the product.<br/>Reads "10/10 would crash again" as negative.
    end

    API->>ES: Bulk index, id = hash(org, product, source, external_id)
    Note over ES: Deterministic id - a replayed job<br/>overwrites instead of duplicating.
    API->>SB: Update job (status: completed, counts)
    API-->>UI: Per-source outcome, not per-video

    UI->>API: GET /analytics and /comments
    API->>ES: Aggregations + top hits per source
    Note over ES: Evidence is balanced across sources.<br/>A global sort returns 100% YouTube because<br/>its scores reach 8843 while Steam scores reach 4.
    ES-->>API: Totals, by_source breakdown, evidence
    API-->>UI: Ranked pain points with citations
    UI-->>User: Dashboard
